Only grouped FP4 quantization, packed-key store, FP4 dequantization and
BF16-query weighted ReLU scoring are adapted. Engine imports, V4.1 RoPE
and double-quantization stages are excluded. The key packer's scale floor
is changed to 6 * 2**-126 before division by 6, matching the original
DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 checkpoint reference. RNE is always enabled by the
provider. The exact Hadamard and fake-quantized BF16 query are prepared
separately; no FP8 substitution or V4.1 query semantics are introduced.
The score kernel retains upstream BF16 rounding points. Python dispatch
uses caller-owned buffers and skips allocation for graph replay.
